cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or these measurements, please cite it as below."
title: "An empirical analysis of Pollard-kangaroo walk constants for interval ECDLP on secp256k1, including the unpublished SOTA family"
authors:
  - alias: Decruptor
    given-names: Decruptor
    notes: "Pseudonymous author."
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-23"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
type: article
abstract: >-
  We report the first independent, large-sample validation of the walk constants
  of the "SOTA" and "SOTA+" kangaroo methods for interval ECDLP on secp256k1 —
  an unpublished family due to RetiredCoder that underlies the fastest publicly
  known solvers for the Bitcoin-puzzle ranges. Using a hash-oracle model of the
  group, we run ~5.1e5 full DLP solves across 70 configurations at interval
  widths 2^31–2^47 and reproduce all published constants within ±0.02; we
  validate and delimit RC's DP-overhead formula, analyze the walk-confinement
  and selection-rule mechanisms behind the constants, and report negative
  results on the mirror second sample and the sqrt(pi/2) "floor" for 1-D walks.
keywords:
  - elliptic curve discrete logarithm
  - Pollard kangaroo
  - interval DLP
  - secp256k1
  - distinguished points
  - Bitcoin puzzle
repository-code: "https://github.com/decruptor/kangaroo-constants"
related:
  - type: isSupplementTo
    note: "ePrint preprint (number pending moderation)"
